{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774195851,"nonce":"UauVjZbAiZV91N2PhX4+UGWB6XI=","title":"Live subagent observation sidebar: partition tracking and activity streaming","message":"When an SDK-spawned session proposes partitions (bigbuild-style) and spawns subagents, the dashboard sidebar should show live progress.\n\n**What it looks like:**\n- When SubagentStart fires, a partition entry appears in the sidebar with agent_id, agent_type, and status\n- Clicking a partition opens a focused view of that subagent's event stream (filtered by parent_tool_use_id)\n- Status indicators: running/completed/errored, with cost and duration when finished\n- Similar to Claude Code's planning outline, but with live streaming of subagent activity\n\n**Infrastructure already in place:**\n- SDKBackend.buildHooks() already registers SubagentStart/SubagentStop hooks\n- subagentTree Map tracks active subagents per session\n- normalizeSDKEvent() processes all SDK message types into ConsoleStreamEvent\n- WebSocket broadcast via storeAndBroadcast() delivers events in real time\n- parent_tool_use_id on messages identifies which subagent produced them\n\n**What's needed:**\n1. Dashboard UI: sidebar component showing subagent list per active session\n2. Event filtering: filter ConsoleStreamEvent by parent_tool_use_id to show focused subagent view\n3. Subagent detail panel: opens as a chat-like view showing the filtered event stream\n4. Status aggregation: derive subagent status from event stream (last event type, result message)\n\n**Interaction with issue 781f473** (subagent result pruning): the sidebar would show the full subagent activity regardless of whether the result sent back to the parent is pruned. This provides observability that would otherwise be lost by pruning.\n\n**Future extension** (depends on SDK-mediated spawning, see companion issue): if subagents are spawned as independent SDK sessions (not via Agent tool), users could interact with them directly — send messages, course-correct, provide input. With Agent-tool subagents, interaction is read-only (observe only).","files":null}]}